<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25786" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lānĭēnus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		lanius, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of a butcher, butcher's</i>: tabernae, Varr. ap.
					<i><span class="en">Non. 532, 20</span></i>.—Hence,
				<i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lānĭēna</span></b> ,
			ae, f.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A butcher's stall</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per myropolia et lanienas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Ep. 2, 2, 15</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lanienae et tabernae conjunctae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					44, 16 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A mangling, dissecting</i>, Prud. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ</span>. 10, 497: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">omnique laniena excruciatus,</span>”
				<i>torture, mutilation</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 29, 1, 44</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
